2. Kubernetes Deployment with Minikube

Download kubectl:
    curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/darwin/arm64/kubectl"

Download Minikube:
    curl -LO https://github.com/kubernetes/minikube/releases/latest/download/minikube-darwin-arm64
    sudo install minikube-darwin-arm64 /usr/local/bin/minikube

Once the installation is complete, start a single-node Kubernetes cluster:
    minikube start

Build the Docker image for the Python website:
    docker build -t python-website:latest .

Load the local Docker image into Minikube:
    minikube image load python-website:latest

Deploy the application using Kubernetes manifests:
    kubectl apply -f deployment.yml
    kubectl apply -f service.yml

Get the service URL to access your application:
    minikube service python-website-service --url
